    "id": "p13-q10",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "The number $5\\square3$ is rounded to 1 significant figure. The answer is 600.\nWhat could the original number have been?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$553$, $563$, $573$, $583$ or $593$; the missing digit can be 5 to 9.",
      "worked": "The first significant figure is 5, in the hundreds place. To round up to 600, the tens digit must be at least 5.\nThe possible original numbers are $553$, $563$, $573$, $583$ and $593$.",
